''Reading.'' The house stands on the registry and the deserializer chain, re-implements the filesystem module's pure half (parity-witnessed against the fork's own module), reads the siting cascades as the adaptor reads them, and answers the kind of a raw tiddler by TW5's own predicates. What it lacks names itself: the disk walker's `tiddlywiki.files` and plugin-folder legs (never needed while `ingest` reads declarations).

''The non-meme round trip'' stands witnessed at `tests/e2e/nonmeme-parity.test.ts`, both doors real; its measured strays read at <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/recipe-layer-model#/owed`>>.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/one-bundle`>>

!! One bundle ~ the caps decide what rings

''The law.'' The route skins, the in-VM face and the engine ship as ONE bundle, and the caps decide what rings (#/rulings).

''What it settles.'' The meme verbs stand as //"the daemon island's skins of the meme laws"//, and //"every skin (this, the HTTP route, the MCP tool) carries verbatim"// one contract, with //"the anchor project[ing] through the in-VM face (`$tw.lares.meme.project`)"// (`packages/lararium-tw5/src/meme-verbs.ts:2-11`). The question stood: do the route skins and the in-VM face ship as ONE bundle, or split by tier. ''They ship as one.'' The route skins, the in-VM face and the engine ride a single plugin, and a vessel's declared cap-stack decides which of them rings on that vessel.

''The three grounds the ruling rests on.''

# ''One law shipped twice reads as two laws.'' The contract every skin carries VERBATIM already reads as ONE law. A split bundle carries it in two artifacts that must be tuned together, and the hand-derived enumeration drifts the way every hand-derived enumeration drifts. One casting rings the same law at the road, the gate and the sanctum; two castings drift by a hair a year and nobody notices until a reader does.
# ''The keel already answers it, for free.'' <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/api/composable-keel`>> `#/absence-is-structural` rules that a Herm reads as //a cap-stack that never declares the wiki cap// and runs //blind by structure, never by a flag a later bug could flip// — //an absent cap grants no authority//. ''One keel, two `#has`-stacks: the same code, thinned by caps, never two codes.'' A bundle split by tier re-spells that thinning in packaging, where the composition root already spells it in wiring — and packaging cannot fail closed. This carrier's own cap posture reads the same direction at docs/pono/recipe-layer-model#/questions: //the cap-stack falls to the floor, never reds//.
# ''What travels stays a cap question, never a bundle question.'' Whether the road-bells — the HTTP route, the MCP tool — ring on a given vessel answers off that vessel's declared stack. A wayfarer that declares no sanctum rings no sanctum-bell, and it does so without a second artifact existing.

''Where the bundle stands.'' `packages/lararium-tw5/plugins/lares-memetic-wikitext.json` ships as ONE plugin tiddler carrying `nalu-engine` and `bag-paths` and no syncadaptor (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/outbound-bridge`>>, `#/island-holds`).

''Where the stories stand.'' The stories that set the intent ride at <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/scale-stories-basket-one`>> `#/one-plugin-or-two`, and the moʻolelo carrying all eight clauses rides at that floor's `#/exit`. ''That floor holds the telling; this carrier holds the ruling.''

⚠ ''What the ruling does NOT settle.'' It fixes the artifact count at one. It says nothing about which caps gate which skin, nor about the manifest shape a thinned bundle presents to a vessel that declares less than the whole. Those stand open here.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/daemon-and-domain`>>

!! Daemon wiki and domain wiki ~ two recipes, side by side

''Two classes, one kernel.'' A ''daemon wiki'' (`recipe: "default"`, slug `daemon`) holds ONE face's memory on ONE device: every slot it writes stays face-private, so it seeds, exports and imports per face (operator, 2026-11-14: //"daemon wikis should seed per-face"//). A ''domain wiki'' (a house wiki: `lares`, `lararium`, `elyncia`, `sdm`, `crossroads`; or one `wiki init` mints, such as `notes`) holds a shared working layer, the realm workbench, which every face its contract seats reads and writes: one document, one folder, one seed (//"most wikis should NOT seed per-face because shared crdts"//). The ''veil floor'' (a vessel wearing no face) stands either class in its own vessel-keyed documents. One `expandRecipe` (`packages/lararium-mesh/src/wiki-recipe.ts`) orders every stack: temp, draft, personal, working, the wiki's canon, the libraries, the wiki's own bag where its canon follows a face, the oracle floor.

| layer (top wins) | daemon wiki (face `F` worn) | domain wiki (`<slug>`) | veil floor (no face) |
|---|---|---|---|
| ''temp'' | `wikis/daemon/temp`: a fresh `MemoryTiddlerStore` each boot; the device alone; mirrors to `<projections>/faces/<pet name>/wikis/daemon/temp/` only under a consent record (`daemonTempMirror`) | `wikis/<slug>/temp`: the same store and life; no mirror unless a consent record names the slug | the same; nothing seals it, nothing carries it |
| ''draft'' | `wikis/daemon/draft`: absent at open (no slot handle, #/as-mounted B), then late-attached as a face's DEVICE slot beside working (`attachDaemonEditSlots`, `packages/lararium-keyhive/src/operator-daemon-behavior.ts:554-581`; `deviceSlot`, `slot-doc-resolver.ts`); mounted writable, never the default write layer; takes the engine's `Draft of …` records by the recipe's own routing; a floor whose rest key does not stand holds it in the island's memory alone | `wikis/<slug>/draft`: a seated face's binding (PersonaGroup × fingerprint), else the vessel's floor doc `wikis/<slug>/drafts/<did>`; no disk mirror (its `recovery/` holds one face's hand) | the DID floor doc, `face-reach: vessel-only` |
| ''personal'' | `wikis/daemon/personal`: absent at open, then late-attached as a face's DEVICE slot the same way; mounted writable, never the default write layer; takes the engine's story list and view-state; face-private on one device, as every daemon slot | `wikis/<slug>/personal`: ONE face's view-state and what it keeps for itself; crosses that face's own devices; projects to `<projections>/faces/<pet name>/personal/<slug>/`; seeds, exports and imports per face; the default write layer for a face that holds no writer's seat in the workbench (`slotLayerFlags` with `writeSlot: "personal"`) | the vessel's floor slot for `personal` (`floorSlot`, `slot-doc-resolver.ts`) |
| ''working'' (the default write layer) | `wikis/daemon/working`: the face's DEVICE slot (`deviceScoped`), late-attached or the boot refuses; written freely by the operator's hand and the AI seat on that device; projects to `<projections>/faces/<pet name>/wikis/daemon/`; refuses every share (`share-face-private`); seeds, exports, imports per face | the REALM WORKBENCH at `realmWorkbenchDocUrl(realm, slug)` (`packages/lararium-mesh/src/deterministic-doc.ts`), the realm a private cabal of one the first face founds (`privateCabalRealmId`, `packages/lararium-mesh/src/workbench.ts`); written by each face seated `admin`, read by each seated `read`; sealed for the realm's roster, each seated face's holder opening it (cabal-realm#/the-workbench); ONE mirror folder: the share entry's workspace, else `<projections>/realms/<realm pet name>/wikis/<slug>`, else `<checkout>/wikis/<slug>` beside a sourced canon; seeds once, exports as one record set | `floor-slot/<slug>/working` in the state document, sealed under the vessel's key; a seat that lands LIFTS its records into the face's workbench, additively |
| ''canon'' | `bags/daemon-<F>` (`daemonFaceCanonBag`): the face's LOCAL canon, minted at its first worn stand, sealed under the face (`standFaceDaemonCanon`); written by the AI's unsigned residency `MOVE` and the hand; projects to `<projections>/faces/<pet name>/bags/daemon/` | `bags/<slug>`: for a house canon slug the Kahu realm's standing document, written live by the Kahu steward alone (`requireKahuReach`) and read by every other face from the floor's snapshot; for a minted wiki the catalog entry's document, written by a holder of its admin cap through an ACTION verb; projects to `<projections>/realms/<realm pet name>/bags/<slug>/` where a mirror grant names it | house canon reads from the oracle snapshots; the daemon wiki at the floor reads no canon (`open-daemon-vm.ts`, no face proved) |
| ''libraries'' | `bags/kahua` first (`kahuaRecipe`): the face's lift-only stage, read-only in the composite, moved only by a signed lift or withdraw; projects to `<projections>/faces/<pet name>/bags/kahua/`; then the vessel's library bags, then `bags/crossroads` (`daemon-vm-core.ts`) | the recipe record's `bag-stack` minus the structural slots, laid at boot and reconciled live (`recipe-watch.ts`) | the floor reads; no private library mirrors (`daemonDiskMirrors` with no face lists crossroads alone, `packages/lararium-node/src/bag-paths.ts`) |
| ''own bag'' | `bags/daemon`: the daemon document (bindings), beneath every library, no mirror | none: a domain wiki's own bag stands as its canon | `bags/daemon` |
| ''floor'' | `bags/oracle`, read-only | `bags/oracle`, read-only; a face outside the Kahu cabal reads house canon here | `bags/oracle` |

''What the table says in one breath.'' The daemon wiki keeps every writable layer on one face and one device, and climbs by two crossings (working -> `daemon-<F>` unsigned, `daemon-<F>` -> `kahua-<F>` signed). A domain wiki shares its working layer across a realm's seats, keeps one face's own layer in `personal`, and climbs to canon by promotion (`MOVE`) or by an offer the Kahu weighs. The veil floor keeps everything under the vessel's own key until a face lifts it.

''The status door agrees with the mount.'' `wiki_status(recipe="default")` lists the daemon composite's own layers (`composite.layerIds`, `packages/lararium-tw5/src/tiddler-verbs.ts`, `makeWikiStatusReactor`), bottom first: `bags/oracle`, `bags/daemon`, `bags/crossroads`, `bags/kahua`, `bags/daemon-<F>`, `wikis/daemon/working` (the one marked `working`), `wikis/daemon/personal`, `wikis/daemon/draft` and `wikis/daemon/temp`. `personal` and `draft` read mounted writable there, as the table's rows say; `temp` reads unwritable through this door, its `why` reading `bag not registered`.

''The browser vessel.'' The same kernel composes the same stacks (`open-browser-vessel.ts`; the daemon recipe at `open-browser-daemon-vm.ts`, its canon under the same `daemonFaceCanonBag` rule); no disk projector runs there, so no layer of either class projects to a folder from a browser.

Two further classes — the derived library and the topic wiki every seated face writes — stand specified and unbuilt; they read at <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/recipe-layer-model#/owed`>>.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/delete-reveals-or-shadows`>>

!! Delete ~ reveal or shadow

''Two acts, one gesture word.'' A title can stand in several layers of one recipe at once, and "delete" can mean two different things there:

* ''REVEAL'' (a retract to absent): the topmost record leaves its own layer entirely. The cascade falls through, and whatever a lower layer holds surfaces. Store primitive: `remove` / `removeInBag` (`packages/lararium-mesh/src/composite-store.ts`). Disk: no shadow file, and a standing one leaves.
* ''KĀPAE'' (a shadow-tombstone, <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/kapae`>> #/core-cut): a tombstone record rises in a writable layer, and every record of the title beneath it stays in its bag yet reads gone. Store primitive: `tombstone` / `tombstoneInBag`; the composite stops at the tombstone (`resolveLayered`, `getLive`). Disk: `<stem>.kapae` where the carrier stood (`packages/lararium-node/src/kapae-shadow.ts`, the projector's `settleShadow`).

Over a title that stands in ONE layer alone, the two acts read the same at the surface and differ beneath: the kāpae stays up and hides any record a lower layer gains later (remove-wins), while the reveal leaves nothing and lets a later arrival show.

!!! The worked case ~ one tiddler in three bags, the user deletes the top

The `elyncia` wiki. Canon `bags/elyncia` holds //Harbor Map// (the table's agreed map); the workbench (`wikis/elyncia/working`) holds the referee's revised map; a player's `personal` layer holds her own annotated copy. She reads her copy, and she presses Delete.

| act | lands | the wiki reads afterward (her face) | the other faces read | a second press |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| ''kāpae'' | a tombstone in `personal`, her own layer | //Harbor Map// gone; working and canon keep theirs, shadowed | unchanged: `personal` crosses her devices alone | answers `absent`: nothing stands to delete |
| ''reveal'' | her `personal` record retracts | the referee's revised map, from the workbench | unchanged | reveals canon only where her face writes the workbench (seated `admin`); seated `read` it refuses `reveal-top-unwritable` |

The same press with the title in canon alone (case c) lands the kāpae in the layer a save would take, at or above working, and a reveal refuses, since her face writes no canon. With the title in the workbench and canon (case b), the kāpae lands in the workbench and shadows canon for every seated face; the reveal retracts the workbench record and canon surfaces for every seated face.

!!! What each door does

| door | case (a) top layer only | case (b) top layer and one below | case (c) below only | names the act |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| the TW5 engine's own delete (the hand in the wiki) | plain: the record retracts from that layer and no kāpae rises, since no layer beneath holds the title (`_leavesAs`, `packages/lararium-tw5/src/island-adaptor.ts`) | kāpae in the top layer, shadowing the lower | kāpae where a save would land: the cascade's layer at or above working, else working (`_tombstoneBag`) | no: the layers decide, plain over nothing beneath and kāpae over a lower layer, so the browser's delete of a canon tiddler keeps it hidden; a layer beneath that the composition could not read counts as holding the title (kāpae): a recipe slot the composer skipped (no reach into that bag, the kahua stage and daemon document a sibling's engine leaves out), named to the composite by `layIslandComposition` (`markUnreached`) and named again after each live reconcile (`recipe-watch.ts`: a library the catalog cannot resolve yet, a slot an oracle move dropped when its new document would not open), and a mounted stand-in for an unread document (a degraded or pending blank, `waitHandle`'s fallback before the real doc merges: `LarTiddlerStore.unknown`), both read through `CompositeStore.unknownBeneath`; a wiki with no working layer refuses by name |
| `delete family=true recipe=<slug>` / `tiddler_delete(family=True)` | plain: the record retracts from that layer | kāpae in the top layer where it stands above the designated bag, else in the designated bag (the tiddler door's layer law, `packages/lararium-tw5/src/tiddler-verbs.ts`) | kāpae in the designated bag (`writable-bag`, the working slot) | no: each member leaves plainly where no layer beneath its landing bag holds a live record, kāpae otherwise; a bag of the stack the island cannot reach counts as holding one (kāpae); the receipt names `tombstoned`, `retracted`, `tombstonedIn` and `readFrom` |
| `delete family=true` on the anchor (`recipe: "default"`) | through the daemon wiki's engine (`wikiMemeSink`, `place-meme.ts`), so the adaptor's law above: plain over nothing beneath | same, kāpae | same, kāpae | no; the receipt names the titles that left under `tombstoned`, since the wiki's shore decides what each leaves as |
| `delete family=true bag=<bag>` | plain: each member retracts from the named bag (`removeMeme` over the bag's sink, which knows its composite's layers: `beneath`, `leaveFamily`) | kāpae in the named bag for each member a lower layer of the composite holds; the rest retract | kāpae in the named bag | no; the receipt splits `tombstoned` from `retracted`; an unread layer beneath the bag in the composite (`unknownBeneath`) counts as holding every member (kāpae). It reads the daemon composite's stack alone, never another recipe that composes the same bag (OWED below). A bag the composite does not mount (a realm steward's, a reached bag, a wiki instance slot) knows no layers beneath and raises kāpae (OWED below) |
| `lares delete` / `tiddler_delete` (the anchor alone) | no mode: a plain delete, the record retracts to absent and no tombstone rises (`mode: "plain"` in the answer); `mode: "kapae"`: tombstone in working; `mode: "reveal"`: retract | no mode: refuses `delete-mode-needed` and names both meanings; kapae: the act names `holds` and `shadowed`; reveal: retract, `reveals` names the lower bag, and a leave reads `revealed-from:<bag>` | no mode: refuses `delete-mode-needed` toward `mode: "kapae"`; kapae: tombstone in working; reveal: refuses `reveal-top-unwritable`, since the layer that holds the record sits beneath working and takes no hand's delete | YES: `mode` (`--mode`) by name wherever a lower layer holds the title, and an unread layer beneath counts as one (`unknownBeneath`): no mode refuses `delete-mode-needed`, and a bare kāpae over it retracts only under `mode: "reveal"` (its act's `reveals` reads `an unread layer`); refuses `delete-mode-unknown` on any other word (`packages/lararium-tw5/src/tiddler-verbs.ts`, `packages/lararium-mesh/src/family.ts`) |
| `lares shore remove` (a pending removal: the file left the bag's own mirror) | plain: the family retracts from the bag whose mirror lost the file, and no kāpae rises (`removeInOwnLayer`, `packages/lararium-node/src/shore-remove-door.ts`) | kāpae in that same bag, shadowing the lower copy, its shadow in that bag's own mirror | — (the record stands in the bag the file left) | no word: the layers beneath that bag decide, and the confirmation names the lower layer; the person's `y` approves the kāpae (`kapae: true`), and without it the answer refuses `remove-raises-kapae`; a layer beneath the composition could not read counts as holding the title |
| `lares act CLEAR` / `DROP` | kāpae over every live title IN the named bag (`executeClear`, `executeDrop`, `action-handler.ts`) | same | — | no: exclusion gestures, kāpae by law |
| `lares act MOVE` (promotion), an INGEST re-link | the source RETRACTS (reveal): the title lands in the target, then leaves the source | same | — | no: relocation, reveal by law |

''A delete deletes plainly; only a lower layer makes it a choice.'' A kāpae earns its place only where a lower layer holds a title the wiki must not surface; regular deletes serve every other case (#/rulings). So the tiddler door, with no mode named, retracts each record to absent: no tombstone rises, no `.kapae` shadow lands on disk, and the pool's history carries a removed file, never a set-aside one. Where a lower layer holds the title too, the door never guesses: it refuses `delete-mode-needed` and names both meanings, since a guess either way breaks something. A reveal there replays the OverlayFS resurrection (kapae#/core-cut): a user who deletes what she reads expects it gone, and a lower copy she never saw surfaces. A kāpae there hides the lower copy, and it also hides every later arrival of that title. ''Each rides by name'': `mode: "kapae"` keeps the lower record hidden (remove-wins under contention: a raised kāpae holds against a peer re-adding a lower copy), and `mode: "reveal"` acts for a hand that wants "discard my layer's version; show me what lies beneath". Every door follows the same rule (the table): plain where no layer beneath holds the title, kāpae where one does. The tiddler door alone takes a `mode` to name the choice; the engine's and the meme door's deletes read it off the layers, since a human deleting in the browser expects a lower canon tiddler to stay hidden. What each door still owes reads at <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/recipe-layer-model#/owed`>>.

!!! The tiddler door's delete, as it stands

* ''What a plain delete moves.'' With no mode named, the door reads the reveal's consequence, and lands it only where every act reveals nothing (`reveals: null`). A record no mounted layer holds (the engine's own) leaves through the live wiki. A lower layer's live record of any member, or a member resting in a layer this face cannot remove it from (`reveal-keeps:<bag>`, `reveal-top-unwritable`), refuses `delete-mode-needed`: the `why` names the layer and the `--mode kapae` / `--mode reveal` choice, and nothing moves.
* ''A kāpae over a title the wiki reads absent.'' Where the wiki reads a title absent and a layer this face writes holds a raised kāpae over it, a plain delete retracts that kāpae to absent (it hid nothing), and the projector lowers its `.kapae` shadow and its record of it, so `lares surface commit` stages the shadow's removal. A kāpae that hides a live lower record retracts only under `mode: "reveal"` (the record surfaces); no mode refuses `delete-mode-needed`, and `mode: "kapae"` answers `absent` (the kāpae it asks for already stands). A root address takes its tombstoned slots with it under `family: true` alone, as a standing family does (`retractBareKapae`, `packages/lararium-tw5/src/tiddler-verbs.ts`).
* ''Which layer takes a delete.'' A layer takes a face's delete only where the island mounts it writable at or above the working layer, and the Kahu predicate and the face's `admin` cap both admit it (`layerFactsFor`). A tombstone shadows only from above, and a canon layer beneath working takes no hand's delete.
* ''What a reveal refuses.'' A reveal retracts the topmost record of the title. Where that record's layer sits beneath working, or the face cannot write it, the reveal refuses `reveal-top-unwritable` and names the layer; a reveal of a record no mounted layer holds (the engine's own, or a wiki with no store beneath it) refuses the same, with nothing to retract. Each refusal names `mode: "kapae"` as the act that would shadow it from working.
* ''A refusal answers a receipt.'' The door answers `decision: "refused"` with `refusal`, `why`, the record's `hash` and the `consequence` it read, and lands nothing; it never throws for a refusal the family law reads. Outside the law the door still throws by name: an unknown mode word (`delete-mode-unknown`), a title that stays home (`tiddler-withheld`; an alert of an open kind under `$:/temp/lares/alert/` reads through the read doors, its named fields alone, redacted of every secret shape, and only by a reader of each record it names; it still refuses here, since the house alone raises and clears it), and a read the face's cap denies. A `$:/` title deletes as any record does.
* ''What the consequence names.'' Each act entry carries `holds` (every layer with a live record of the title) and, by mode, `shadowed` (the layers a kāpae hides) or `reveals` (the layer that surfaces, `null` where none does or a kāpae stands there). The `leaves` entries give each reason in `why`: `revealed-from:<bag>` for a title that a lower live record now answers, `reveal-keeps:<bag>` for a fellow family member whose layer this hand cannot write and which therefore stays as it reads, `stands-beneath:<bag>` for a record that stays in a layer this hand cannot write, beneath the tombstone that shadows it. `versions` names the titles the consequence itself names (the target, each act, each leave, each orphan) and no other, so an answer stays bounded on a wiki of any size.

!!! A family takes one mode, as one change per layer

A meme's root and its component slots leave together (the family law, `packages/lararium-mesh/src/family.ts`, `consequence`): one `mode` covers every member, the consequence reads before anything lands, and each layer takes its members as ONE change (`writeFamily`). The tiddler door refuses a root or slot (`tiddler-delete-in-a-family`, with the consequence) unless the call names the family act (`family: true`, `--family`), and refuses a slot its parent calls by `kahea` even with the flag (the parent's text moves through the put on the parent). Cross-layer atomicity cannot exist: a family split across two layers lands as ordered writes, one per layer. the delete naming `family=true` on the anchor reads the same consequence, lands one change per member through the daemon wiki's engine (`removeMeme`, `wikiMemeSink`), and takes no mode: the engine's layers decide, plain over nothing beneath and kāpae over a lower layer (the mode word for a reveal over a lower layer stays owed, road `L37`).

!!! How each act travels

| road | kāpae | reveal |
|---|---|---|
| sync | a tombstone record in its document, crossing wherever that document crosses: the workbench to its seated faces, `personal` to one face's devices, the daemon working layer nowhere beyond its device slot | a key leaves its document, crossing the same way |
| disk mirror | `<stem>.kapae` replaces the carrier file (`settleShadow`, `disk-projector.ts`) | the carrier file leaves; no shadow; a standing shadow leaves |
| seed (re-founding) | the mirror's `.kapae` raises the kāpae again through INGEST, remove-wins inside one wave (`seed-mirrors.ts`; `action-handler.ts`, the kāpae an export's shadow files name) | nothing to carry: the folder holds no file |
| export / import | the daemon working layer's `.kapae` files carry as `kapae` records (`commands/house-bundle.ts`); a workbench's import wave raises them (`wiki-working`, the `kapae` tally) | nothing |
| offer toward house canon | carries nothing: the offer reads the face's view and offers live titles alone (`offerSourceOf`, `canon-offer-verbs.ts`) | nothing |
| promote (`MOVE` of one title) | ''the delete crosses into canon'': a tombstoned source lands a tombstone IN the target and retracts its own (the tombstone road, `executeMove`), and refuses where the target holds nothing unless the hand asks `--shadow` | — (MOVE itself reveals its source) |
| promote (`MOVE` of a whole layer) | skips every tombstone: a layer promotion carries no kāpae (`executeLayerMove`) | — |
| the kahua stage | no kāpae: the stage takes no tombstone; a signed `withdraw` retires an item (kahua-memory-stage#/the-lift), and a daemon-working kāpae over a lifted title shadows it on that device alone (the shadow shows its diff) | — |

!!! How a hand reverses each

* ''A reveal'' reverses by a put: the hand writes the record back into its layer (the version it read stands in the consequence's `versions`).
* ''A kāpae'' reverses two ways: a put of a live record over the tombstone replaces it (the hand's new record then shadows the lower copy in its turn), or the tiddler door retracts the tombstone record itself: a plain delete where it hides nothing, `mode: "reveal"` where a lower copy surfaces. Neither LOWERS it in the kapae#/law sense: no effect record audits the retract. `lares wiki resolve <title>` reads which layers hold the title and which tombstone hides it (`makeResolveReactor`, `worker-data-verbs.ts`).

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/rulings`>>

!! Rulings

# Operator ruling (the recipe strata), verbatim at <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/recipe-layer-model#/ruling`>>: for each recipe the top bag follows the KIND of raw tiddler — the named wiki bag for most, a drafts layer above it, volatile per-device tiddlers on top, the canon bags beneath.
# Operator rulings, verbatim at the same slot: a draft doc fleet-syncs where a PersonaGroup sync-fleet cap stands and falls to the device floor where none does; `personal` keeps its own layer; `meme get --recipe` reads "the stack"; every wiki mounts a `working` layer, the daemon included; `draft.of` drives the draft switch (operator ruling 2026-09-11).
# Operator ruling 2026-09-11 (Basket-One slot 8): "one bundle, the caps decide what rings" (#/one-bundle); the stories that set it rest at <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/scale-stories-basket-one`>> #/one-plugin-or-two.
# Operator ruling 2026-11-14: daemon wikis seed per face; domain wikis share one CRDT and seed once (#/daemon-and-domain); the ask stands verbatim at <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/recipe-layer-model#/owed`>>.
# Operator ruling 2026-11-20, verbatim (quote license): "that doesn't read pono to kapae -> only needs a shadow-tombstone-kapae if there's a tiddler underneath you don't want to surface when deleting one out of a bag with more priority, i.e. multiple bags with the same title and you need that title 'not to appear' in the rendered wiki after the kapae action. Regular deletes serve most other cases." (#/delete-reveals-or-shadows)
# Operator ruling 2026-11-26, the canon floor by place: `lares` in every wiki, `lararium` and `lares` in the herm/hearth wiki, and TiddlyWiki5's native docs (`tw5-docs`, `tw5-dev`) beneath them there (#/canon-floor-by-place).
# Operator ruling 2026-11-21 (the ever-speaking present): the model lifts from the docs record to this api meme (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/ever-speaking-present`>>).

